  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "The component 'Animator Locomotion Control' which (according to the documentation) restricts movement in desktop and VR, does not function to disable player movement when applied in my animators (Tested in Action and FX animator layers so far).\n\nWhen viewed in the in-game avatar Debug, the status of the Locomotion override seems to start as Disabled for one frame but then stays as Enabled.\n\nI will be testing this in Base layer soon and report back, and if it works then this should be noted either as a bug, or, if intentional behavior, as incomplete documentation, as the page does not state a specific layer to use for its functionality.\n\nEDIT 1: Simple public test avatar ID:\n\navtr_1df63aba-d184-457a-acb8-3b1ed11c8431\n\nThe animator on it is set up in such a way that you should have 0 movement ability.",
